Quick heads up -- I just merged the connection pooling fix (PR #4502).

Before the fix, each v2 request was opening a new DB connection because
the pool wasn't being reused across the middleware chain. Under load
this caused connection exhaustion after ~800 concurrent requests.

After the fix, we're reusing connections properly and I tested up to
3,000 concurrent requests without issues. Pool size is set to 50
connections per instance (configurable via DB_POOL_SIZE env var).

This was the last P0 blocker for the migration. All P0s are now resolved.

Remaining P1 items:
 - Pagination cursor encryption (to prevent parameter tampering)
 - Request body size limit per endpoint (currently global 10MB)
 - GraphQL-style field selection for GET endpoints

P1s can be done post-cutover.

- Bob

